    "case_for": "The fluctuation relations identify a precise, general link between microscopic dynamics and macroscopic thermodynamics, including far-from-equilibrium processes. Evans and Cohen established an early theorem, while Jarzynski and Crooks developed influential relations connecting nonequilibrium work to equilibrium free energies. Their results are exact, experimentally testable, and now standard across statistical physics; their importance does not depend on a particular device or application.",
    "case_against": "The ballot groups related but distinct results, so a prize must define the central achievement and distinguish the contributions of Evans, Jarzynski, and Crooks from other work in nonequilibrium statistical mechanics. Its broad conceptual reach may also be less immediately visible than the impact of some experimental platforms.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson argued that quantum error correction made reliable quantum information processing physically conceivable, while noting that large-scale fault tolerance remains incomplete.",
        "response": "I agree that this is a foundational advance, and the unfinished engineering does not erase its conceptual importance. The fluctuation relations make a similarly fundamental contribution by stating what irreversibility permits in small, fluctuating systems. I favor them here because their scope is sharply expressible as exact results with mature theoretical and experimental use; the error-correction case requires weighing foundational codes against a still-developing computing program."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson emphasized that WMAP turned broad cosmological questions into tightly constrained measurements, while flagging the challenge of dividing credit among mission leadership, instrument builders, and the wider analysis team.",
        "response": "The precision and lasting influence of WMAP are strong reasons to consider it. Its large mission and analysis effort makes individual attribution a central difficulty. For B026, the key theoretical contributions are more readily tied to specific named results, though the distinct formulations still need careful historical comparison."
      }
